WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.880
With 2017's Thor: Ragnarok, director Taika
Waititi gave us something completely different

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:12.120
from the previous two Thor films, showing
us places and characters unlike anything else

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.210
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:20.170
The fantastic visuals and rapid-fire jokes
were enough to dazzle movie fans of any age.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:25.480
But while kids might be satisfied with spectacle,
once older viewers really start thinking about

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.640
the movie, there are more questions than answers
- especially once you factor in the events

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.730
of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:38.760
Here's a spoiler-filled look at some Thor:
Ragnarok details that only adults notice.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.570
Odin stinks at hiding things

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:46.899
The key villain for most of Ragnarok is Hela,
the Goddess of Death who also happens to be

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:51.330
Thor and Loki's older sister, and the oldest
child of Odin.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:57.079
Hela, it turns out, was banished by Odin,
hidden away in a secret prison until his death

00:00:57.079 --> 00:00:58.780
abruptly frees her.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.239
Suddenly, the secret ain't so secret, which
is actually a recurring problem for Odin throughout

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:09.850
the Thor franchise, as the All-Father is apparently
really bad at hiding things.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.829
In the first film, it was the secret of Loki's
Frost Giant birth.

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:17.779
In the second, it turns out there was a secret
portal out of Asgard.

00:01:17.779 --> 00:01:21.729
Now here comes a daughter that he apparently
never told his sons about.

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:27.109
And in all three cases, once the secret got
out, people got killed.

00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:33.179
If Odin were a little better at hiding these
things, Asgard might still exist today.

00:01:33.179 --> 00:01:34.719
Where is Sif?

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:39.700
Both of Thor's leading ladies from the previous
films are suddenly and mysteriously missing

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.189
in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:45.609
Jane Foster's absence is explained with a
single throwaway line saying she and Thor

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:46.619
broke up.

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:51.350
That's a pretty casual dismissal for a star
as big as Natalie Portman, but it's nothing

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:57.200
compared to what Jaimie Alexander's Lady Sif
gets - which is, in fact, literally nothing.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:02.119
Aside from an actress playing her in the drama
Loki stages commemorating his own death, Sif

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:04.459
isn't even mentioned in Ragnarok.

00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:09.090
In the real world, Alexander apparently had
a scheduling conflict, but in Ragnarok, she

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.220
just vanishes and nobody really seems to give
a crap.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:17.930
Marvel later piled on even more, with Avengers:
Infinity War directors Joe and Anthony Russo

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.989
revealing she died offscreen in Infinity War.

00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:22.709
Seriously, guys?

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.909
Who is on Doctor Strange's watch list?

00:02:25.909 --> 00:02:30.680
Though the film spends less time on Earth
than either previous Thor adventure, Ragnarok

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:36.040
does depict Thor and Loki's unexpected encounter
with Doctor Strange, who traps Loki in a pocket

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.129
dimension while he has a chat with Thor about
why they've come to Earth.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.709
"I keep a watch list of individuals and beings
from other realms that may be a threat to

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:44.709
this world.

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:47.790
Your adopted brother Loki is one of those
beings"

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.670
It's a fun scene, but it makes you wonder:
who else is on that watch list?

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.959
Is Doctor Strange the Marvel equivalent of
the TSA?

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:01.000
We have a feeling we haven't seen the last
of this mysterious watch list of his.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.670
Thor: god of… nothing?

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.670
In addition to extreme strength, durability
and a lifespan much longer than that of a

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.100
human, Thor is the God of Thunder, which is
a key plot point in Ragnarok.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.590
"Are you Thor, The God of Hammers?"

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.950
"That hammer is to help you control your power,
to focus it.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.440
It was never your source of strength"

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:28.439
So if his body is naturally gifted with the
power to channel lightning, why is he so vulnerable

00:03:28.439 --> 00:03:29.439
to shocks?

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:34.269
He gets shocked by a net thrown on him by
scavengers when he first arrives on Sakaar,

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:38.739
and then is repeatedly zapped by the neck
implant placed on him by Valkyrie after she

00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:39.890
captures him.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:44.000
Maybe those don't run on normal electricity
or something, but it's weird to see him get

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.299
shocked in one scene and then pull a lightning
storm out of the sky in another.

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:51.909
Valkyrie has a drinking problem

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:56.459
The first time we meet Valkyrie, she falls
off her ship after taking a big drink.

00:03:56.459 --> 00:04:00.820
The moment is played for laughs, as are other
moments involving Valkyrie and alcohol, but

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:05.840
as the story plays out we find she is using
alcohol to block traumatic memories of her

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.190
friends being slaughtered by Hela.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:12.930
Though her addiction is mostly played for
laughs, when viewed as a whole, Ragnarok actually

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:17.600
presents a tragic view of a woman trying to
drink herself into oblivion.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.640
Where is Asgard exactly?

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:25.860
In the first Thor film, the Bifrost is the
only way to get to and from Asgard, which

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.780
is why it's such a tragedy when it is destroyed.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.950
In the second movie, though, we learn there
are actually secret portals that sometimes

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.720
allow travel to and from Asgard as well.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:36.730
Okay, fine.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:42.360
In Ragnarok, though, all bets are off, as
people seem to be able to come and go at will,

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.050
simply flying spaceships to and from Asgard.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.780
Apparently, the rules for traveling to Asgard
work however the plot needs them to at any

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:54.240
given moment, as seemingly anyone can just
drive there if they want.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.700
So… road trip, anyone?

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.900
Infinity what now?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:04.270
Speaking of all those Asgardians on that spaceship,
Avengers: Infinity War begins shortly after

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:09.410
Ragnarok left off, with the Asgardian refugee
ship destroyed by Thanos.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:14.210
In the carnage, we see the loss of numerous
Asgardians, but we don't know anything about

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.870
what happened to Valkyrie or Korg.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:22.180
In a Q&amp;A at an Iowa high school of all places,
though, Infinity War co-director Joe Russo

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:26.120
revealed that Valkyrie survived, along with
half the Asgardians.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.479
So where are they?

00:05:27.479 --> 00:05:32.210
Well, one clue might be hiding in plain sight
at the end of Ragnarok, as the Grandmaster's

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:36.840
pleasure cruise vessel, battered but still
recognizable, can be seen parked on top of

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.610
the larger refugee ship.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:42.819
It's not big enough to hold everyone, but
Valkyrie could certainly fit - and maybe even

00:05:42.819 --> 00:05:44.960
have room to bring Korg with her.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:45.770
Here's hoping!

